7. The suit was admitted on 17-9-2006. On the same date, predicated both on the fact that the plaintiff&#39;s claim arises out of non-receipt of expenses on account of the freight, demurrage, private monitoring charges, Chittagong Port Authority (&#39;CPA&#39;) electricity and monitoring charges, CPA store rent, destruction cost, survey fees and other expenses totaling Taka 46,04,531.51 and that should the plaintiff be ultimately found to be entitled to a decree in the suit it will have no recourse for satisfaction of the decretal amount, this Court on the plaintiff&#39;s prayer directed the defendant No. 1 to furnish security for the claim amount of 46,04,531.51 by way of a bank guarantee through a schedule bank in Bangladesh. Pending the furnishing of such security by the Defendant No. 1, this Court also directed the proforma defendant No. 4 the Commissioner of Customs, Customs House, Chittagong not to allow the defendant No. 1 to export its goods from Bangladesh. Further by an Order dated 4-10-2006 this Court, noting that the defendant No. 1 having taken no steps to furnish security for the plaintiff&#39;s claim as earlier directed by this Court, was seeking instead to proceed against the plaintiff further to a Legal Notice dated 28-8-2006, upon an application for temporary injunction filed by the plaintiff issued a notice to show cause upon the defendant No. 1 and pending hearing of that application directed the defendant No. 1 by an order of ad-interim injunction to refrain from taking any action in pursuance of the said Legal Notice.&nbsp; 

 (4) Is the plaintiff entitled to any decree against the defendant? If so, to what extent ?&nbsp; 

 The instant Admiralty Suit is thus liable to be decreed in favour of the plaintiff for a sum of Taka 32,28,703 equivalent to US$ 47,134.35 inclusive of cost ex parte against the defendant No. 1. Hence it is ordered that the Suit be decreed ex parte against the Defendant No. 1. The plaintiff gets a decree for. Taka 32,28,703 (Taka thirty-two lac, twenty-eight thousand, seven hundred and three) only inclusive of cost with interest @ 13% per annum on the decretal amount assessed from the date of the institution of the suit till the date of the realisation of the decretal amount. The decretal amount shall be realised from the defendant No. 1.&nbsp;
